.TH "CSSFONTFACEDESCRIPTORS" "3JS" "March 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSFontFaceDescriptors \- CSSFontFaceDescriptors
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSFontFaceDescriptors\f[B]\f[R] interface represents a
CSS declaration block for an \f[CR]\(atfont\-face\f[R] at\-rule.
.PP
Each descriptor in the body of the corresponding
\f[CR]\(atfont\-face\f[R] at\-rule can be accessed using either its
kebab\-case property name in bracket notation or the camel\-case version
of the property name in dot notation.
For example, you can access the \f[CR]font\-family\f[R] CSS descriptor
as \f[CR]style[\(dqfont\-family\(dq]\f[R] or
\f[CR]style.fontFamily\f[R], where \f[CR]style\f[R] is a
\f[CR]CSSFontFaceDescriptors\f[R] instance.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] The \f[CR]CSSFontFaceRule\f[R] interface represents a
\f[CR]\(atfont\-face\f[R] at\-rule, and the
\f[CR]CSSFontFaceRule.style\f[R] property is an instance of this object.
.RE
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Inherits properties from its ancestor
\f[CI]CSSStyleDeclaration\f[I].\f[R]
.PP
The following property names, in kebab\-case (accessed using bracket
notation) and camel\-case (accessed using dot notation), each represent
the value of a descriptor in the corresponding \f[CR]\(atfont\-face\f[R]
at\-rule:
.TP
\f[B]font\-display\f[R] or \f[B]fontDisplay\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]font\-display\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]font\-family\f[R] or \f[B]fontFamily\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]font\-family\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]font\-feature\-settings\f[R] or \f[B]fontFeatureSettings\f[R]
A string representing the value of the
\f[CR]font\-feature\-settings\f[R] descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]font\-stretch\f[R] or \f[B]fontStretch\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]font\-stretch\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]font\-style\f[R] or \f[B]fontStyle\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]font\-style\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]font\-weight\f[R] or \f[B]fontWeight\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]font\-weight\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]font\-width\f[R] or \f[B]fontWidth\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]font\-width\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]size\-adjust\f[R] or \f[B]sizeAdjust\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]size\-adjust\f[R]
descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]src\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]src\f[R] descriptor.
.TP
\f[B]unicode\-range\f[R] or \f[B]unicodeRange\f[R]
A string representing the value of the \f[CR]unicode\-range\f[R]
descriptor.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]No specific methods; inherits methods from its ancestor
\f[CI]CSSStyleDeclaration\f[I].\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Accessing \(atfont\-face descriptor values
This example defines a \f[CR]\(atfont\-face\f[R] rule and then uses
\f[CR]CSSFontFaceDescriptors\f[R] to read back the descriptor values.
.SS CSS
.IP
.EX
\f[B]\(atfont\-face\f[R] {
  \f[B]font\-family\f[R]: \(dqMyHelvetica\(dq;
  \f[B]src\f[R]:
    local(\(dqHelvetica Neue Bold\(dq),
    local(\(dqHelveticaNeue\-Bold\(dq),
    url(\(dqMgOpenModernaBold.woff2\(dq) format(\(dqwoff2\(dq);
  \f[B]font\-weight\f[R]: bold;
  \f[B]font\-style\f[R]: normal;
  \f[B]font\-display\f[R]: swap;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] myRules = document.getElementById(\(dqcss\-output\(dq).sheet.cssRules;
\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] rule \f[B]of\f[R] myRules) {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (rule \f[B]instanceof\f[R] CSSFontFaceRule) {
    \f[B]const\f[R] style = rule.style; \f[I]// a CSSFontFaceDescriptors\f[R]
    log(\(gafont\-family: ${style.fontFamily}\(ga);
    log(\(gasrc: ${style.src}\(ga);
    log(\(gafont\-weight: ${style[\(dqfont\-weight\(dq]}\(ga);
    log(\(gafont\-style: ${style.fontStyle}\(ga);
    log(\(gafont\-display: ${style[\(dqfont\-display\(dq]}\(ga);
  }
}
.EE
